The following test files in Cassandra's
test/unit/org/apache/cassandra/cql3/statements directory, which this
directory mirrors, were not translated:

* DescribeStatementTest.java: almost all its tests compare the full output
  of DESCRIBE statements, including all the table and keyspace options, the
  list of system keyspaces and the exact formatting - all of which differ
  between Scylla and Cassandra, and even between Cassandra versions. Scylla's
  DESCRIBE is tested in test_describe.py instead.
* AddIdentityStatementTest.java and DropIdentityStatementTest.java: test
  Cassandra's ADD IDENTITY and DROP IDENTITY statements, used by Cassandra's
  mTLS authenticators, which Scylla doesn't have. They also check the results
  through Cassandra's internal role manager.
* CreateRoleStatementTest.java, AlterRoleStatementTest.java and
  CreateUserStatementTest.java: parse statements through Cassandra's internal
  parser and check the parsed objects - the options of Cassandra's network
  authorizer (ACCESS TO DATACENTERS) and CIDR authorizer, which Scylla
  doesn't have.
* PropertyDefinitionsTest.java and SelectStatementTest.java: test Cassandra's
  internal PropertyDefinitions and SelectStatement classes directly, through
  Java APIs.
* TransactionStatementTest.java and TxnDataNameTest.java: test Cassandra's
  Accord transactions (BEGIN TRANSACTION), which Scylla doesn't have.
